      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see the point about \"just deserts\" and maintaining order. However, if we look at the empirical outcomes, many argue that retributive systems actually fail to deter crime and instead disproportionately target marginalized communities, which seems to undermine the \"rule of law\" they claim to protect. \n\nGiven that, can we truly say retributive justice is a \"cornerstone\" of a fair society, or is it more accurate to view it as a fundamentally regressive mechanism that we are simply struggling to outgrow?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
